# AndersonTech IAM Lab — Entra ID Module

A hands-on identity and access management lab built to demonstrate practical
Microsoft Entra ID (Azure AD) administration and automation skills, alongside
a companion on-premises Active Directory environment.

This repo covers the **cloud-native Entra ID portion** of the lab. The
on-premises AD side (OUs, security groups, GPOs) was built separately in
`andersontech.local` and is documented in a sibling repo/section.

## Why two separate labs instead of one hybrid environment

The original plan was a fully hybrid setup (on-prem AD synced to Entra ID via
Entra Connect). Entra Connect installation was blocked in the cloud-hosted
environment used for this lab, so the two pieces were built and documented
independently instead:

- **On-prem AD lab** — OU structure, department security groups, Group
  Policy Objects (screen lock, Control Panel restrictions, account lockout
  policy)
- **Entra ID lab (this repo)** — cloud-native users, groups, licensing-aware
  security controls, and Graph API automation

Documenting *why* the hybrid sync didn't happen, rather than hiding it, is
intentional — troubleshooting real environment constraints is itself part of
the IAM story.

## What's in this lab

| Area | What was built | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Users | ~40 users created via bulk CSV import | Mirrors the department structure from the on-prem AD lab |
| Groups | Static security groups per department (SG-IT, SG-Sales, etc.) | Assigned membership — dynamic membership requires Entra ID P1 |
| Security Defaults | Enabled tenant-wide MFA enforcement | Free-tier alternative to Conditional Access, which requires P1/P2 |
| Roles | Scoped built-in role assignment (e.g., Groups Administrator limited to a specific group) | Demonstrates least-privilege without requiring PIM (P2) |
| App registration | Registered a sample app (`AndersonTech-UserAuditTool`) with `User.Read.All` delegated permission only | Least-privilege applied to application permissions, not just users |
| Logging | Reviewed Audit Logs and Sign-in Logs for traceability | Included as screenshots in `/screenshots` |

## Licensing notes (worth knowing, not just working around)

Entra ID Free tier does **not** include Conditional Access, PIM, Access
Reviews, or dynamic group membership — those require P1 or P2, and even the
free trial of P2 requires a credit card for identity verification. Rather
than activate a trial, this lab deliberately stayed on Free tier and used
the closest equivalent capability at each step (e.g., Security Defaults
instead of Conditional Access). The gaps are documented here rather than
glossed over, since knowing exactly what a licensing tier unlocks is itself
a relevant IAM operations skill.

